# Notary — Project Rules

## 1. Tech Stack & Versions
- Go 1.23+
- CLI framework: github.com/spf13/cobra v1.8+
- Embedded DB: modernc.org/sqlite (pure-Go, no CGO) v1.30+
- Signing: stdlib crypto/ed25519
- Config: stdlib os.Getenv + github.com/joho/godotenv (dev only) v1.5+
- Testing: stdlib testing + github.com/stretchr/testify v1.9+
- Target integration: Mem0 via its REST API (net/http directly, no official Go SDK)
- Optional LLM phrasing: an OpenAI-compatible chat-completions provider (net/http, no provider SDK added), export path only, never the write path

## 2. Folder Structure
notary/
├── cmd/
│   └── notary/
│       └── main.go                  # CLI entrypoint (Cobra root command)
├── internal/
│   ├── record/                      # Structured reason-record schema + hash-chaining
│   │   ├── record.go                # Includes the VisibilityTier type
│   │   └── chain.go
│   ├── store/
│   │   └── sqlite.go
│   ├── sign/
│   │   └── sign.go
│   ├── interceptor/
│   │   ├── interceptor.go           # The pluggable Interceptor interface + fail-mode config
│   │   ├── observer.go              # The shared Observer: library and proxy build the same records
│   │   ├── library/
│   │   │   └── mem0.go              # LibraryInterceptor
│   │   └── proxy/
│   │       ├── proxy.go             # ProxyInterceptor (Phase 9)
│   │       └── pipeline.go          # The bounded write queue: queue, writer goroutine, drop tally, drain
│   ├── export/
│   │   └── export.go
│   └── replay/
│       └── replay.go
├── config/
│   └── config.go
├── go.mod
├── go.sum
└── README.md

## 3. Coding Style
- Standard Go error handling, never panic in library code
- Exported types/functions get doc comments
- Naming: camelCase unexported, PascalCase exported, snake_case only for SQL columns
- File length guidance: aim under ~300 lines per file as a signal to split by responsibility, not a hard ceiling
- No global mutable state — pass dependencies explicitly through constructors

## 4. Error Handling
- Every fallible function returns an error; never swallow one silently
- Wrap errors with context: `fmt.Errorf("writing record: %w", err)`
- Never log key material or raw sensitive memory content
- CLI errors surface in plain language, full detail behind `--verbose`

## 5. Guardrails
- Do NOT install new dependencies without asking first
- Do NOT touch files outside the current phase's scope
- No hardcoded secrets or signing keys anywhere in the repo — env vars or OS keychain only
- No refactoring of working code from a prior phase unless explicitly asked
- The structured record is always the source of truth — no code path may treat LLM-generated text as authoritative
- `VisibilityTier` must be a type that cannot be constructed without specifying its value — no code path may write "observed" data through a path that could also write "reconstructed" data
- Every write to the store must be idempotent from Phase 4 onward
- The audit-observation path defaults to fail-open-loud; nothing in v1 implements fail-closed, since v1 has no enforcement function
- In proxy mode, a failure in the audit-write path must never block, delay, or fail the underlying Mem0 request/response